# The archives this build is allowed to download, each named by the release it
# is published under, because the same file name is reused release after
# release. The format is the one `sha256sum` writes, so an archive can be
# checked by hand with `sha256sum --check` from the folder it was downloaded to.
#
# A download that hashes to something else stops the build. When a tool version
# changes, add its lines here as well: `cargo xtask` prints the line to add,
# with the digest of what it just downloaded, and it is worth comparing that
# against what upstream publishes before pasting it in.
#
# The binaryen digests below are the ones published beside each archive as
# `<archive>.sha256`. WASI SDK and Typst publish none, so those were taken from
# the archives themselves.

